{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The platform's own trip record puts the waiting time at well under the free period. The free waiting period started at 2026-09-03T09:12:01 (wait_timer_started) and the trip started at 2026-09-03T09:13:39 (started_at) - 98 seconds - and the record's own wait_time_min field reports 1.7 minutes (about 102 seconds). Both are below the 180 second free waiting period this record carries in platform_policy.free_wait_sec. Under POL-NS-10(d) a waiting-time fee of platform_policy.waiting_fee_sgd is chargeable only where the trip was completed AND the driver's in-geofence dwell before the rider boarded, measured as POL-NS-01(c) measures it, exceeded free_wait_sec; under POL-NS-10(e) a waiting-time line that limb does not support is refunded in full. The $5.00 line fails the condition on the record's own timestamps.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02740", "EV-FARE-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-10", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The GPS trace confirms the shortfall independently of the platform timer, and by the same clock POL-NS-01(c) prescribes. The driver's longest qualifying in-geofence run is 100 seconds: 11 consecutive fixes (fix_count 11) from 09:11:59 to 09:13:39, the last fix coinciding with the moment the trip started. The derived shortfall against the 180 second minimum is 80 seconds (shortfall_basis 'longest_run_sec'). So the dwell the rider must pay for is 100 seconds, not 180. The point survives on any figure in the record: the derived threshold block reports minimum_dwell_sec of 180 seconds for this STANDARD pickup, and even the stricter 300 second STANDARD figure retained in the fee schedule leaves the 100 second run short.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02740", "EV-TRIP-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-10"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver cannot stretch the clock by summing separate intervals. POL-NS-06(i) permits dwell to be accumulated across in-geofence intervals only where a traffic_advisory that is present and populated covers the pickup road and carries a type of KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT. EV-ADVIS-02740-01 is MISSING: it carries issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0 and no payload, and the derived arrival block records advisory_candidates as empty with a single in-geofence interval (run_count 1, accumulated_dwell.limb.available false). POL-NS-06 states in terms that a MISSING traffic_advisory makes limb (i) unavailable. This claim relies on that artifact only for its absence, which the brief makes citable; nothing is asserted against it, and the weight of 0.0 is disclosed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02740-01", "EV-GPS-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.limb.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The platform-confirmed-arrival route does not rescue the charge on this trip. POL-NS-12 applies only where trip_record.platform_policy.arrival_marker is GPS_AUTO and the record carries the platform's own arrival event stating its geofence test together with wait_timer_started and wait_timer_expired events. This record's arrival marker is BUTTON, the arrival event is the driver's own 'I'm Here' tap at 09:11:59, and there is no wait_timer_expired event anywhere in the trip record. POL-NS-12 is therefore outside the case and the dwell question is decided on the exported trace, which gives 100 seconds.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-12", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.platform_policy.arrival_marker",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The wait was not the rider's doing, and the fee's condition does not turn on rider conduct at all. The rider track shows 241 fixes, all 241 of them qualifying, every one of them within the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius (maximum distance 7.36 m from the pin) and all at 0.0 kph, and the rider sent 'coming' at 09:12:19 (read at 09:12:29) before boarding at 09:13:39. POL-NS-10(d) conditions the waiting-time fee exclusively on the driver's own in-geofence dwell before the rider boarded, which was 100 seconds; no limb of POL-NS-10 makes the fee chargeable because the rider took slightly longer than the free period to appear.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02740", "EV-CHAT-02740", "EV-TRIP-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-10"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's answer is 'The app added it automatically' - an account of how the line was generated, not evidence that the 180 second waiting period was served. The party who asserts that money is owed carries the burden of proving the facts that make it owed (POL-GEN-07(1)), and nothing on this record supplies the missing 80 seconds: the trip record's timer, the trip record's wait_time_min and the GPS dwell all say the same thing, and no advisory exists to explain or extend the wait. The charge is therefore unsupported, and where the condition for a charge is not established the amount is returned to the party who paid it (POL-GEN-07(2)).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02740", "EV-FARE-02740", "EV-GPS-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-07", "POL-NS-10"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.wait_time_min",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The remedy is arithmetic and it is the whole of the contested sum. The amount contested is $5.00, which is exactly the waiting_time_fee line the fare breakdown carries and exactly platform_policy.waiting_fee_sgd in force for the trip; payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.0, so the entire contested amount is still collected and untouched. POL-NS-10(e) refunds that line in full, which returns the whole contested amount to the filing rider and makes the outcome FULL_REFUND under POL-GEN-03. No driver compensation arises on this record, because the free waiting period the fee is consideration for was never served.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02740", "EV-TRIP-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-10", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.waiting_time_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver did reach the pickup point on this trip, and the trace verifies it: the derived arrival block of the GPS record counts 11 qualifying fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, the first at 09:11:59, so the proximity test in POL-NS-02 is satisfied and the fact of arrival is not open to dispute.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02740", "EV-TRIP-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 'I'm Here' tap at 09:11:59 is a true arrival marker, not a false one: the first qualifying in-geofence fix carries the same timestamp, the driver's track closes to 0.65 m of the pickup pin, and the driver was stationary in that run, so neither trigger of POL-NS-05 - being more than 300 m from the pin, or travelling at 15 km/h or more - is met. The waiting clock was correctly started by platform telemetry at 09:12:01 and no false-arrival referral should be entered against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02740", "EV-TRIP-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.first_ts",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This case is decidable on clean evidence: the trip record's arrival event and the nearest trace fix agree to the second, well inside POL-NS-08(a)'s 90 second clock-skew threshold; the trace reports 100.0% coverage with an empty gaps list and a 0 s maximum gap; and the single chat message matches trip_record.chat_message_count of 1. No artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08, so the judge should fix the facts on the record rather than escalate.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02740", "EV-TRIP-02740", "EV-CHAT-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own profile shows no fee-farming pattern that could justify withholding anything from him or escalating against him: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 67, so the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip, and no other profile field may be substituted into that test (POL-GEN-01).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The $5.00 line is the platform's own published waiting fee for this trip, not a figure the driver selected: the platform_policy in force records waiting_fee_sgd of 5.00 and the fare breakdown's waiting_time_fee is 5.00, with the ledger reconciling to total_charged of 33.23, so the amount itself is correct and no billing-integrity defect of the kind POL-NS-08(d) describes arises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02740", "EV-FARE-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-10", "POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.waiting_time_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Candidly, the qualifying in-geofence run on this record is 100 seconds, running from the first in-geofence fix at 09:11:59 to the trip start at 09:13:39, against the free waiting period of 180 seconds in force for this STANDARD pickup (PLATFORM-PUBLISHED-2026-10-07); measured as POL-NS-01(c) measures it, that dwell does not exceed the free period, so the driver does not resist refund of the $5.00 waiting line under POL-NS-10(d) and (e). He asks only that the ruling record the arrival as genuine, enter no false-arrival referral against him, and attach no adverse finding to a charge the platform applied automatically.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02740", "EV-TRIP-02740", "EV-FARE-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-10", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not a wrong-entrance or pin-ambiguity case: the pickup is a single registered pickup point at a recorded venue (VEN-YISHUN-RING, registered_pickup_points = 1), and the rider's own derived track sits within 7.4 m of the pickup pin with zero recorded speed, so the parties were at the same recorded location and no POL-NS-03 goodwill payment arises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02740", "EV-GPS-02740"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.max_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
